{"title":"Career Roadmap · Molecular Diagnostics Technician","role":"Molecular Diagnostics Technician","summary":"A Molecular Diagnostics Technician performs laboratory procedures that detect, identify, or characterize genetic material and molecular biomarkers associated with infectious diseases, inherited conditions, cancers, and other diseases. The role combines molecular biology, laboratory technology, genetics, diagnostic workflows, quality control, and increasingly automation and bioinformatics.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Molecular Diagnostics Technician performs laboratory procedures that detect, identify, or characterize genetic material and molecular biomarkers associated with infectious diseases, inherited conditions, cancers, and other diseases. The role combines molecular biology, laboratory technology, genetics, diagnostic workflows, quality control, and increasingly automation and bioinformatics."},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the direct pathway within the supplied category is a recognized B.Sc/B.Sc (Hons.) Medical Biotechnology, Molecular Biology, Medical Laboratory Technology with appropriate molecular-diagnostics training, Biotechnology, Genetics, or a closely aligned program. A generic BPT or BOT degree does not automatically qualify a graduate for molecular diagnostic laboratory work."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical work environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Molecular diagnostic laboratories"},{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Genetic testing laboratories"},{"text":"Pathology laboratories"},{"text":"Public-health laboratories"},{"text":"Cancer diagnostic centres"},{"text":"Research institutes"},{"text":"Biotechnology companies"},{"text":"Clinical research organizations"},{"text":"In-vitro diagnostics companies"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","h